  'depot.photos.go_btn': 'Download pictures from Google Photos…',
  'depot.photos.go_hint': 'Takes you to the Photos page, where you pick which account and which pictures come down. That is the only place you download from — come back here to see what landed in the depot.',
  'depot.photos.title':          'My photos on this computer',
  'depot.photos.what_html':      '<strong>What is this for?</strong> The photos you pick in Google Photos <strong>come down to your computer</strong>, into the depot — a separate folder per account. Once a photo is here it stays available offline, and you open it in your file manager like any other file.<br><strong>They land in one place only.</strong> The download writes straight into the depot — there is no in-between location to move them from later. If the depot is not set up or is unreachable, the download <strong>does not even start</strong>; it tells you what to set up.<br><strong>This is an import, not a sync:</strong> unlike Drive, nothing goes <strong>back</strong> to Google Photos. What you delete here <strong>stays</strong> up there; what you delete up there <strong>stays</strong> here. Picking the photos is always yours to do, on the <strong>Photos</strong> page.',
  'depot.photos.where_html':     'On your computer the folder is named <strong>after the account</strong> — photos from <code>lackor2</code> go into <code>System/Storages/GOOGLE_PHOTOS/lackor2</code>. You do not rename it, so two accounts can never mix.',
